### CareSync-Specific Cross-Browser Concerns

The project's `playwright.config.ts` defines 5 browser/device projects: `chromium`, `firefox`, `webkit`, `mobile-chrome` (Pixel 7), `mobile-safari` (iPhone 13). Use these as the canonical browser matrix.

* **Supabase Auth flow**: OAuth redirects and email/password login behave differently across browsers (especially Firefox and WebKit). Test the full login → dashboard redirect in all three desktop browsers.
* **`react-day-picker`**: Date picker rendering and keyboard navigation differ between Chromium, Firefox, and WebKit. Test date selection in all three.
* **`@radix-ui/react-select` / `@radix-ui/react-popover`**: Popper positioning engine (`@floating-ui`) can render dropdowns clipped in Firefox if the portal root is not handled correctly. Verify dropdowns open upward/downward as needed.
* **`react-dropzone`**: Drag-and-drop behavior varies; tap-to-click must work on mobile Safari (WebKit) where drag events are not supported.
* **`framer-motion` animations**: Easing and transition timing differ subtly between browsers; verify no animation hangs or leaves elements in a broken state.
* **`sonner` toasts**: Verify toast dismissal and stacking behavior in Firefox (which sometimes ignores `duration`).
* **`next-themes`**: Verify no flash of unstyled content (FOUC) and no `hydration mismatch` console warnings in any browser.
* **Print styles**: The discharge summary and lab result print paths must be tested via `print` emulation in Chromium and Firefox.
* **Font rendering**: Inter / system-ui fonts render differently; verify no text overflow or clipping in tabular data (vitals, lab values, medication doses).

